.TH IMPROV-SERVER 1 "" "improv" "Improv Manual"
.SH NAME
improv\-server \- JSON HTTP API over an Improv model
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBimprov\-server\fR [model] [addr]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B improv-server
serves one model over HTTP/1.1 as JSON: read the model and measures, compute
what-if edits through the live engine, and write input cells. It listens on
.I addr
(default 127.0.0.1:3000, or
.BR IMPROV_ADDR ).
.I model
defaults to
.IR improv.db .
.PP
A model is a store file made by
.BR improv (1),
or a Postgres model URL,
.BI postgres:// user @ host / db ?model= name\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
[\fImodel\fR] [default: improv.db]
The model: a store file, or postgres://USER@HOST/DB?model=NAME
.TP
[\fIaddr\fR] [default: 127.0.0.1:3000]
The address to listen on
.SH ROUTES
Every route is served under
.I /v1
and, as an alias, without it.
.I /v1/openapi.json
describes them.
.nf
GET  /v1/health                 liveness, no token needed
GET  /v1/openapi.json           the OpenAPI document, no token needed
GET  /v1/model                  the whole model
GET  /v1/measures               id, name, kind, categories
GET  /v1/measures/:id/values    stored inputs or computed values
POST /v1/measures/:id/eval      what-if edits; "persist": true writes through
POST /v1/measures/:id/cells     set one input cell (write scope)
POST /v1/nl/parse, /v1/nl/describe
                                controlled English to formula and back
GET  /v1/scheduler/status       refresh scheduler state
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR IMPROV_API_TOKEN ", " IMPROV_API_TOKENS
Write-scope bearer tokens (one, or comma-separated).
.TP
.B IMPROV_API_TOKENS_RO
Read-scope bearer tokens (comma-separated).
.TP
.B IMPROV_API_TOKEN_FILE
A file of
.IB name : scope : secret
lines,
.I scope
being
.B read
or
.BR write .
.TP
.B IMPROV_MAX_BODY_BYTES
Request body limit (default 1048576).
.TP
.B IMPROV_RATE_LIMIT
Requests a minute per token, or per client address without one (default
600; 0 turns it off).
.TP
.B IMPROV_AUDIT_LOG
Append the write audit log (one JSON object per line) to this file instead
of standard error.
.TP
.B IMPROV_ALLOW_OPEN=1
Allow running without a token on a non-loopback address (otherwise the
server refuses to start).
.TP
.B IMPROV_SCHEDULER=1
Refresh external-function measures in the background. It runs only functions
whose digest is listed in the file named by
.BR IMPROV_EXTFN_ALLOW .
.TP
.B IMPROV_ADDR
The address to listen on when no
.I addr
argument is given.
.TP
.B IMPROV_EXTFN_ALLOW
The allowlist file for the scheduler: one lowercase hex SHA-256 of
.IR name \e0 body
per line.
.TP
.B IMPROV_SCHEDULER_TICK_SECS
The scheduler's tick period (default 5).
.TP
.B IMPROV_HEADER_TIMEOUT_MS
Header read timeout (default 10000).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
IMPROV_API_TOKEN=secret improv-server sample.db
curl -H 'Authorization: Bearer secret' localhost:3000/v1/measures
.fi
.SH AUTHOR
Greg Burd <greg@burd.me>
